ormation for Client About Notice of Completion of Limited Scope Representation (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-11/fl955info.pdf)\nciteturn1687search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.1 years ago; Crawled: 9.1 years ago;    When you and the limited scope attorney signed the *Notice of Limited Scope Representation* (form FL-950), you agreed to sign the *Substitution of Attorney—Civil* (form MC-050) when the attorney completed the tasks listed on form FL-950. ... But, if you can’t, YOU MUST ACT RIGHT AWAY to file papers and ask for a court hearing. ... Form FL-956 is also available online at courts.ca.gov/documents/fl956.pdf.\nFL-955-INFO — Information for Client About Notice of Completion of Limited Scope Representation\n\n1. **Why did I get this Proposed Notice of Completion of Limited Scope Representation (form FL-955)?**  \n   When you and the limited scope attorney signed the *Notice of Limited Scope Representation* (form FL-950), you agreed to sign the *Substitution of Attorney—Civil* (form MC-050) when the attorney completed the tasks listed on form FL-950.  \n   You have not yet signed that *Substitution of Attorney* form. By serving you a Proposed *Notice of Completion* (form FL-955), your attorney is telling you that he or she has completed the tasks agreed to and is taking action to be removed from your case.\n\n2. **Why is it marked “Proposed”?**  \n   The attorney wants to give you a chance to respond if you agree or disagree that he or she completed the work for you.\n\n3. **What do I do if I agree?**  \n   You can contact the attorney and say that you agree. But you don’t have to take any action.\n\n4. **What if I don’t take any action?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=1&query=civil)\nciteturn1687search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without