il a copy of the form to the other parties in your case. The person who mails your form is called a server.\n\n    * Before mailing, your server should fill out the rest of page 2. They do not sign the form yet.\n    * Make enough copies of the form for yourself and any other party in the case.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1687search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * CIV-100 * Request for Entry of Default (Application to Enter Default) Effective: January 1, 2023 ...   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSP09-03 \nInvitation to Comment \n | SP09-03 Invitat (https://www.courts.ca.gov/partners/documents/comment.pdf)\nciteturn1687search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; MC–050 ... COURT ORDER—CIVIL\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=1&query=SC-)\nciteturn1687search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=11&query=DE-)\nciteturn1687search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: January 1, 2009\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=12&query=TH-)\nciteturn1687search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * MC-050 * Substitution of Attorney—Civil (Without Court Order) Effective: